When enableArrayMethods() is enabled, immer does not always commit nested drafts, resulting in illegally accessing revoked proxies. This happens when copying an existing draft object and then adding it back to the array via mutation.

Repro:
  enableArrayMethods();
  const oldState = [{ nestedArray: [] }];
  const newState = produce(oldState, (state) => {
    const newVal = { ...state[0] };
    state.push(newVal);
  });
  newState[1].nestedArray.length; // throws: illegal operation attempted on a revoked proxy

Observed: newState[1].nestedArray is a revoked proxy, indicating the draft was not committed. Expected: the nested draft is committed and reading it works.
